    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d426">

                <pb facs="0766" n="662" sameAs="frus:frus1943CairoTehran/pg662"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Hopkins
                    Papers</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Prime Minister’s Assistant Private Secretary</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Brown</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the President’s Special
                        Assistant</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hopkins</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left"><hi rendition="#small-caps">most secret</hi>
                        <lb/>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">most immediate</hi></seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Cairo</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1943-12-02">December 2, 1943</date>.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p rendition="#flush"><hi rendition="#small-caps">Mr. Hopkins.</hi></p>
                <p>The Prime Minister has instructed me to send down to you immediately, for the
                    President’s information, the attached copy of telegram No. 365 from Angora to
                    the Minister of State, Cairo, which was repeated to Teheran and which the Prime
                    Minister saw last night, and of telegram No. 394 from Angora to the Embassy at
                    Cairo which has just been received.</p>
                <closer><signed>F. D. W. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Brown</hi></signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p rendition="#flush">2.12.43</p>
                </postscript>



